    "answer": {
      "short": "$A=(\\ln4,\\,4\\ln4-4)$\n\nSet $y'=0$ at the maximum, then substitute into the original function.",
      "worked": "At the maximum, $y'=0$. Since $y'=4-e^x$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\n4-e^x&=0\\\\\ne^x&=4\\\\\nx&=\\ln4\\\\\ny&=4\\ln4-e^{\\ln4}\\\\\ny&=4\\ln4-4\n\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $A=(\\ln4,\\,4\\ln4-4)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
